title An eleventh clean cold-run survey, eight reds now that build_target closed
prompt The inner prompt's rite: round-open, claim check, cold run held fully still, build, send, log.
think Round-opened clean at f16de489c9; the dead-letter box named seven parked stashes, two fold shelves, and four moved entries, all elder and already recorded by prior laps.
think Checked the claim board -- five standing rows, all past six-hour expiry, no overlap.
think Read HEAD once (f16de489c9) and launched the cold run with --cadence-slice 1, then held fully still -- no commit, edit, or pull -- across six Monitor re-arms until run_verdict= landed, roughly 65 minutes.
think Closed clean: tree_moved=no, run_verdict=guard_red (the roster's own expected self-check), 371 green, 8 red, 3 gated.
think The eight reds (standing_equipment_redleg, shim_reason, query_wire_retention, ceiling_teeth, ignored_walk, rye_compiled_reach, falsifier_form_outcome, standing_equipment) and the three gated (rule_twin, pond_enclosure_policy, pond_enclosure_ephemeral) matched the standing untriaged list exactly -- one fewer red than the prior ten laps, since the last lap's build_target pen-conversion repair (mantra_bolt_apply_step_witness moved off its fixed path) closed that guard for good rather than merely re-confirming it.
think Read this lap's council-rota row: git rev-list --count HEAD = 6763, 6763 mod 5 = 3, so row 3, Water -- tastes. Its own teaching is to taste up close rather than trust a stamped citation -- run the actual command, sip the actual transcript. Applied to the survey itself: the transcript's own per-guard lines were read directly (grep for red-line verdicts) rather than trusted from the summary count, confirming the drop from nine reds to eight was the real build_target closure and not a miscount.
think No REDS row booked -- nothing crossed the bounded single-lap ratchet test this time.
obs The fleet's untriaged residue is now six items (query_wire_retention %756, ceiling_teeth's asserted_only population, ignored_walk's tree-walks-past-git ceiling, rye_compiled_reach's uncompiled-body ceiling, falsifier_form_outcome's 21 falsifier-less ranked rows, shim_reason's unrostered-swallow ceiling) -- one smaller than the ten-lap standing count, and each remaining item still wants Keaton's word or a plan larger than one lap affords. The prior lap's build_target repair is the proof that this residue is not uniformly stuck: a pen-conversion lap closes a guard for good when one is actually scoped and taken.
file recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md why appended this lap's next entry with the cold-run reading, the rota row, and the shrunk untriaged count
file session-output/standing-equipment-cold.txt why the cold run's own transcript, read for its run_verdict and per-guard verdicts
recommend check-in (either) -- eleven consecutive clean confirmation laps, now down to six standing reds after the last lap's real repair; the residue wants Keaton's word (a pen-conversion plan for rye_compiled_reach, a ceiling decision for ceiling_teeth and query_wire_retention, a falsifier-writing pass for falsifier_form_outcome) rather than a twelfth survey.
status GREEN -- round-open clean, claim board clear, cold run held fully still to run_verdict=, next section updated, log committed with the work.
